HST Office: HST Writer, HST Sheets, HST Slides and HST PDF open in windows of their own; a document tab
can be moved into a new window; autorecovery restores the windows and tabs.
Owner decisions (12/11 and 13/11/2026): "HST Office" (the Start Center) keeps one window with every
document as a tab. The HST Writer/Sheets/Slides/PDF launchers and documents opened from a file manager
open as a tab of the window of their module used last, or in a new window of the module; never in the
HST Office window or another module's window. Inside a module window, File > New / File > Open / "+"
of the same module add a tab; a document of another module goes to that module's window (or a new
one). With only the HST Office Start Center open, a launcher keeps the Start Center and opens its own
window. Dragging a tab out of the strip, "Move to New Window" in its context menu or in View, or
Ctrl+Alt+Shift+N (.uno:DetachDocumentTab) moves it into a new window.
Design (framework/inc/documenttabgroup.hxx): DocumentTabGroup manages several tab groups, each of kind
"office" or a module key (writer, calc, impress, draw, pdf, other module ids).
- Routing of a frame about to be shown: Start Center -> an HST Office window; opened from outside (LoadEnv
  Referer private:OpenEvent, set by DispatchWatcher for every command line/IPC request: launchers with
  --writer/--calc/--impress, Windows shortcuts and open verbs, Linux .desktop %U, macOS Finder; also read
  from the model when SfxFrame::Appear shows the frame first) -> the module's window used last, else a
  new one; otherwise the window the user works in (Desktop active frame, else the group used last) when
  it accepts the module (HST Office accepts all), else the module's window, else a new one. The first
  window of the process is an HST Office window. LoadEnv passes the module of a frame without component
  (SvtModuleOptions::ClassifyFactoryByURL, PDF type -> HST PDF). A frame shown for the load progress
  before its document exists is routed when LoadEnv prepares it.
- LoadEnv recycling: a document from outside never replaces the Start Center or a document of an HST
  Office window, except the Start Center macOS shows before a launcher's first document (tdf#41775,
  desktop app.cxx marks it); that window becomes the module's window.
- "+" offers the module's new document and Open in a module window (Open only for HST PDF/Draw), every
  application in the HST Office window. Next/PrevDocumentTab and the title-bar close act on the window of
  the frame. A second "soffice" without arguments (HST Office launcher) brings an HST Office window to the
  front or opens a new Start Center (desktop app.cxx, Appear event); .uno:ShowStartModule (macOS Dock
  click) opens a Start Center window when only module windows exist (startmoduledispatcher.cxx).
- Detach: a window with 2+ tabs, not in full screen; the new window has the kind of the old one, the
  restored size of the old one and its top-left at the drop point (menu/command: cascaded). Drag within
  the strip reorders; a drop on the strip of another window that accepts the module moves the tab there
  (not on Wayland, where window positions are unknown). Inactive tabs are shown on release. The drop
  uses the system pointer position (motion outside the window is not delivered everywhere).
- Autorecovery: the layout (window kind, tab order, shown tab, window state; documents by URL, new
  documents by title) is written to hst-document-tabs.txt in the backup folder after every change and
  removed on a normal quit; AutoRecovery rebuilds it for the recovered documents (old data: as before).
- Taskbar identity (TitleBarUpdate::updateApplicationID): tabs of an HST Office window use the Start
  Center id (HST Office), module windows their module id.
- vcl: hst_vcl_set_tab_group(window, group id); macOS joins native full screen tabs of the same group only.
- Menus: View > "Move to New Window" in Writer, Calc, Impress and Draw; Ctrl+Alt+Shift+N (Global).
- Vietnamese strings for the new texts.
License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-module-windows.py under Xvfb; tests/unit/test_module_window_groups.py.
